		{
			"id": "evqr8fhRKsJI2fwIE",
			"description": "Bolt Pistol, Mk II Phobos-Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Phobos-pattern bolt pistol is a common Astartes sidearm, its grip and slide machined to mag-lock against a suit of power armour's thigh or chest plate when holstered. Codex background across many Chapters shows it as the Techmarine-serviced companion to the chainsword for close-quarters work once a boltgun's magazine runs dry.\n\nDesign: The Astartes-scale pistol round: 5dx2(2) pi++ with a 2d+2 cr ex follow-up, the same dice and divisor as the Godwyn-De'az pattern above but with the Astartes pi++ wounding and full follow-up that pattern gives up for a human hand (see its design). Handling: an Astartes-proportioned pistol per the framework's rule that Astartes-pattern wargear is built heavier than its human counterpart, not merely relabelled - 8 lb loaded (vs the human Godwyn-De'az's 5 lb) for a larger case, reinforced slide and servo-assisted grip sized to a gauntleted hand. Min ST 13† (√(10×8)≈9, bumped up for the same recoil-handling reasons as the human pistol) means a Space Marine (ST 30, well over 1.5×13) fires it one-handed with no penalty, while an unaugmented human cannot even lift it to the two-handed standard. Acc, range, RoF, Shots, Bulk and Rcl are unchanged from the human pistol - same mechanism, just a bigger housing and the heavier Astartes round. LC0 because, per the framework's legality table, Astartes-marked wargear is heresy for the unauthorised to possess even though the mechanism is identical to a human-issue bolt pistol.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
