		{
			"id": "eJpv79TAI4NzKObMj",
			"description": "Heavy Bolt Pistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Fielded by Primaris Space Marines (Bladeguard Veterans, Inceptors and others), current Codex background is explicit that the heavy bolt pistol fires a larger case than the legacy bolt pistol, closing most of the gap with a full boltgun in a sidearm's frame.\n\nDesign: \"Heavy\" is taken literally: it is given the full Godwyn boltgun anchor damage (6dx2(2) pi++ / 3d cr ex follow-up) rather than the reduced pistol line above, on a bigger frame with a magazine (14 rounds) between the standard pistol's 8 and the boltgun's 24. Handling: at 9 lb loaded it is heavier again than the Phobos-pattern Astartes bolt pistol (8 lb), for the larger case the Codex describes; min ST 13† follows the same Astartes-pistol logic as the Phobos-pattern above (√(10×9)≈9.5, bumped for recoil). Range and Acc sit above the lighter bolt pistol because the larger case gives a flatter trajectory and better sight radius; Bulk -3 (one step worse than the standard bolt pistol's -2) reflects the bigger frame, and Rcl 3 is unchanged since the case is bigger but the mechanism is the same.",
