		{
			"id": "emzRaBn2b0xGn7afM",
			"description": "Boltgun, Umbra Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Umbra is a Heresy-era pattern name; the differences from the Godwyn anchor here (a heavier, more conservatively built receiver kept in service out of reliability and reverence rather than performance) are this project's own and are not attested in a specific source.\n\nDesign: Fires the same standard .75-calibre mass-reactive bolt as every other weapon on this page, so the damage line is identical to the Godwyn-pattern anchor (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex); the pattern difference is manufacture and furniture, not ballistics. Handling: this is a full Astartes-pattern boltgun, built for ST 30 hands and far heavier than any human weapon - per the framework's own worked figure (an Astartes Godwyn boltgun is about 35-40 lb loaded, Deathwatch lists 18 kg), and the older, thicker-walled Umbra receiver runs 3 lb over that anchor at 41 lb. Min ST 20 (√(10×41)≈20) is well above what a Guardsman can shoulder without a heavy penalty, but a Marine at ST 30 clears 1.5×20=30 exactly, letting him fire it essentially one-handed in a pinch, as the fiction shows. Bulk -5 (one step worse than a human rifle's -4, per the framework's Astartes-pattern rule) reflects the longer, heavier receiver; Rcl 3 and RoF 3 (semi/burst, per framework.md's boltgun mechanism note) and the 24-round sickle magazine are unchanged from the Godwyn anchor, since none of that differs pattern to pattern - only the housing does.",
