			"local_notes": "Lore: Phobos is a Heresy-era pattern name; the lighter, shorter receiver relative to the Godwyn and Umbra lines is this project's own differentiation (no source is claimed), without any suggestion it hits softer.\n\nDesign: Same anchor damage (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex) as every standard boltgun; only the housing moves, reflecting a newer, more compact build rather than a different cartridge. Handling: still an Astartes-scale weapon, but the shortest and lightest of the legacy patterns at 34 lb (4 lb under the Godwyn anchor). Min ST 18 (√(10×34)≈18.4) follows from that lighter housing, and Bulk improves to -4 - the same figure a full-size human rifle carries - for the shorter receiver, one step better than Umbra's or Godwyn's -5. RoF, Rcl and the 24-round magazine are unchanged; a lighter pattern doesn't fire a different cartridge.",
