		{
			"id": "e5gtDpCEtQ3heTVO-",
			"description": "Boltgun, Sororitas/Human Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Not every boltgun-armed Imperial servant is a Space Marine: Adepta Sororitas Battle Sisters, Inquisitors, commissar-general staff and other elite, unaugmented humans are shown across Black Library and Codex background wielding full boltguns despite lacking Astartes-grade strength - the recoil is punishing and the weapon a real handful, but never depicted as literally unliftable the way an Astartes boltgun would be for an ordinary Guardsman. This entry gives that human-scale weapon its own line rather than folding it silently into the Astartes-pattern stat block above, per the framework's rule that human- and Astartes-scale versions of the same weapon type need different min ST and weight, not just a relabelling.\n\nDesign: Unlike a bolt pistol scaled down for a human hand, this is a full-length rifle firing a genuinely smaller-calibre round with a lighter mass-reactive charge than the Astartes-pattern .75-calibre shell - it needs a smaller case to keep recoil survivable for an unaugmented shooter shouldering a rifle rather than the Astartes anchor's rocket-assisted cartridge, so wounding drops from pi++ to pi and the frag follow-up shrinks from the anchor's 3d cr ex to 1d+2 cr ex. Dice and armour divisor are otherwise unchanged from the Astartes anchor (6dx2(2), divisor (2)), so penetration odds against DR are identical to the Godwyn Pattern's own figures: 79.4% against carapace (DR 70, effective DR 35), 45.4% against Sororitas power armour (DR 85, effective DR 42.5, the armour this weapon's own wearers actually fight in), and 14.5% against Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective DR 50, unchanged by the armour rescales) - a human-scale bolter still reliably punches through carapace and can hurt another Sister of Battle roughly half the time, but the lighter charge and smaller frag load mean a hit that does get through a Marine's plate does less of the \"several bolts to kill another Marine\" damage the full Astartes round manages. Handling: built to roughly half the Astartes anchor's loaded weight, per the framework's explicit guidance (\"a human-scale boltgun roughly half that\" of the ~38 lb Astartes figure) - 19 lb loaded, a lighter alloy stock and shortened housing rather than a different mechanism. Min ST 14 (√(10×19)≈13.8) is still well above a standard lasgun's ST 9, reflecting a genuinely heavy, hard-recoiling weapon for an unaugmented human - a Guardsman-strength user (ST 10-11) fires it at a real but survivable under-ST penalty, unlike the Astartes-pattern guns above which are effectively unusable by anyone that light. Bulk -4 matches a human rifle of this size (one step better than the Astartes pattern's -5, since there's simply less gun to carry); RoF 3, Rcl 3, Acc 4 and the 24-round sickle magazine are unchanged from the Astartes-pattern anchor, since the action and cartridge are identical - only the stock is cut down.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adepta Sororitas",
				"Inquisition",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
