			"id": "e04iv4uFM7RpyaR6k",
			"description": "Boltgun, Mk IV Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Mk IV pattern name comes from Heresy-era sources; the simplified, mass-production character given here (cheaper to produce in bulk than the Godwyn or Umbra lines, at some cost to finish) is this project's own and is not attested in a specific source.\n\nDesign: Same anchor damage (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex); the only intended difference from Godwyn is manufacture quality, reflected in cost, not a performance edge. This project does not model a reliability penalty for it (no Malf value is given anywhere in this file), since the fiction never quantifies one; a GM wanting to dramatise \"mass-production and less reliable\" can assign a house Malf rating without touching these numbers. Handling: still a full Astartes-pattern boltgun - a slightly plainer receiver shaves 2 lb off the Godwyn anchor's 38 lb rather than changing the gun's class, landing at 36 lb (min ST 19, √(10×36)≈19, unchanged from the anchor at this rounding). RoF 3, Shots 24(3), Bulk -5 and Rcl 3 all match the Godwyn anchor exactly - a mass-production line is cheaper to build, not a different weapon to fire.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
