		{
			"id": "e88TUlcwXp_B9owzP",
			"description": "Storm Bolter",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Twinned boltgun barrels sharing a single trigger and (usually) a large drum or box magazine, standard wargear for Terminator squads and a common pintle/hull weapon on Imperial vehicles; Codex and Horus Heresy background consistently shows it as simply \"two boltguns fired together,\" not a more powerful round.\n\nDesign: Same .75-calibre bolt and therefore the same damage line (6dx2(2) pi++ / 3d cr ex follow-up, identical to the standard Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern's penetration checks) as the Godwyn anchor; \"rof: 3x2\" captures the twin-linked barrels doubling the effective volume of fire per the standard GURPS convention for linked weapons. Handling: two full boltgun actions and a bigger drum magazine make this noticeably heavier than a single Godwyn-pattern gun - 40 lb loaded, roughly two barrels' worth of receiver sharing one stock and trigger group rather than twice the weight of one gun. Min ST 20 (√(10×40)≈20) sits a point above the single-barrel anchor, and the 60-round magazine matches the larger drums shown in art and background (Shots 60(3)). Bulk -6 (one step worse than a single boltgun's -5) and Rcl 4 (up from 3) reflect the twin barrels' combined mass and kick. Listed here for infantry use (built for ST 30 hands, minimum ST 20; Terminators carry it) with Guns (Rifle); a vehicle- or turret- mounted storm bolter should instead use Gunner (Machine Gun) per the framework's skill table, with no change to the damage line.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1900",
