		{
			"id": "enj1cYEf6TAJv6hqL",
			"description": "Storm Bolter, Sororitas/Human Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Adepta Sororitas (Retributor squads, Immolators, Repressors), Inquisitorial retinues and Guard vehicle crews use twin-barrelled storm bolters rather than the Astartes-scale weapon above; the hardware is the same idea, sized for unaugmented hands.\n\nDesign: The human-scale counterpart of the Storm Bolter: the same relationship the Sororitas/Human boltgun has to the Godwyn Pattern. Two Sororitas/Human boltgun actions share a stock, so the damage line is that gun's (6dx2(2) pi, 1d+2 cr ex follow-up), penetrating carapace 79.4%, Sororitas power armour 45.4% and Astartes Mk VII 14.5% per hit. Handling: 20 lb loaded, about half the 40 lb Astartes weapon (framework: human-scale is roughly half); min ST 14 (√(10×20) ≈14) (two-handed, †). Bulk -5 (one worse than the human boltgun's -4 for the twin barrels) and Rcl 4 mirror the Astartes storm bolter's step up from a single gun. RoF 3x2 and the 40-round magazine (a smaller drum than the Astartes 60) follow the same twin-linked convention. A vehicle- or turret-mounted one should use Gunner (Machine Gun).",
