		{
			"id": "e4H1nPzgeJl4u1HPp",
			"description": "Heavy Bolter",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's standard support-weapon bolter, tripod- or vehicle-mounted, firing an oversized bolt round; consistently shown chewing through infantry and light vehicles alike while remaining useless against a main battle tank's frontal armour.\n\nDesign: This is the project's second fixed anchor: 7dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 4d cr ex (exact dice distribution computed with a Python script, not just averages). Checked against the vehicle armour table: AV10 (DR 100, e.g. a Sentinel or a Chimera's side) has effective DR 50 against the armour divisor (2); 7dx2 averages 49 and penetrates 41% of hits, \"chewing\" light vehicles about 40% of the time as required. AV11 (DR 150, Rhino front/sides, effective DR 75) drops to 0.1%, and AV12-14 (DR 200-350) are effectively 0%, so it does not reliably hurt medium- or heavy-armoured vehicles - both outcomes match the assignment's check. Against a suit of Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective DR 50) it penetrates the same 41% of hits, and it essentially never beats a Terminator (DR 200, effective DR 100) - a support weapon that threatens infantry and armour alike but not the heaviest plate. Handling: an oversized cartridge and a tripod-grade receiver put this at 85 lb loaded, close to Deathwatch's own figure for the weapon (roughly 40 kg with its mount). Min ST 14B: the \"B\" (bipod/tripod) marks that the mount, not the gunner's back, bears most of that weight, so the ST figure covers recoil control rather than the raw sqrt(10×85)≈29 a shoulder-fired weapon this heavy would need - comparable to the similarly mounted Autocannon (85 lb, ST 14M) elsewhere in this project. RoF 8 follows framework.md's explicit \"heavy bolter around 8\" guidance - a genuine sustained-fire support weapon, faster than an infantry boltgun's semi/burst RoF 3 but well below a true chain-driven autoloader. Bulk -7 and Rcl 4 mark a support weapon needing a mount or a very strong shooter (only Astartes or a braced tripod). Shared pattern: Astartes Devastators and Guard heavy-weapon teams field the same weapon on the same mount, so it is one stat block rather than a human/Astartes split.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
