		{
			"id": "ehva59lZ6SVXemgvz",
			"description": "Bolt Rifle, Primaris Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Introduced with the Primaris Space Marines, current Codex background describes the bolt rifle as firing a slightly more powerful cartridge with improved sights and effective range compared with a legacy boltgun, without claiming it is a different order of weapon.\n\nDesign: One pip over the Godwyn anchor (6d+1x2(2) pi++, read as (6d+1)x2 as GCS does: the multiplier applies to the whole roll; follow-up 3d cr ex) for the \"more powerful cartridge\" the Codex claims, plus a real jump in Acc (5 vs 4) and range (300/1200 vs 200/1000) for the improved optics and barrel. Magazine capacity (20) sits below the legacy boltgun's 24 to reflect the bulkier round in the same-size housing. Against Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective DR 50) the extra pip nudges the average from 42 to 44 and raises penetration from the standard bolt's 14% to about 21% (exact dice distribution) - a small but real edge from the \"more powerful cartridge,\" most visible against exactly the kind of target (power armour) the Codex text is describing. Handling: a lighter, more refined Astartes-pattern build than the legacy line - Codex background credits Primaris weapons with improved engineering, modelled here as 22 lb loaded against the legacy Godwyn's 38 lb, still very much an Astartes-scale weapon and nowhere near a human-portable one. Min ST 15 (√(10×22)≈14.8) follows from that lighter housing. Bulk -4 (one step better than the legacy Astartes pattern's -5) matches the sleeker, more modern silhouette Codex art gives it; RoF 3 keeps the standard boltgun cyclic rate (it's a designated-marksman pattern, not an assault weapon - see the Auto Bolt Rifle below for that role), and Rcl 3 is unchanged.",
