		{
			"id": "eYsHQeD5CdFO7yKhH",
			"description": "Auto Bolt Rifle, Primaris Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Primaris pattern optimised for volume of fire over range, background material frames it as trading the bolt rifle's reach for a much higher cyclic rate, closer in role to an assault weapon than the standard bolt rifle's designated-marksman feel.\n\nDesign: Standard Godwyn-anchor damage (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex; the cartridge itself is not upgraded, unlike the Primaris bolt rifle above) with RoF doubled to 6 and a bigger 30-round magazine, at the cost of Acc and range falling below even a legacy boltgun to reflect the shorter, gas-hungrier barrel that lore says trades reach for volume. Handling: same lighter Primaris-pattern housing as the Bolt Rifle above (24 lb loaded, min ST 15, √(10×24)≈15.5), with a shorter barrel and a bigger feed mechanism to sustain RoF 6 rather than the standard pattern's semi/burst RoF 3 - a genuine mechanism difference, not a relabelled rifle, per lore's framing of it as closer to an assault weapon. Bulk -4 and Rcl 3 match the Bolt Rifle's figures, since the extra rate of fire comes from the feed and action, not a heavier or more awkward gun.",
