		{
			"id": "e-3zdcRJirOB-HDjz",
			"description": "Stalker Bolt Rifle, Primaris Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A single-shot precision bolt rifle firing subsonic ammunition, a marksman option for Primaris Intercessor-type squads and covert kill-teams; background stresses stealth and one-shot precision over rate of fire. (Which squads carry it is medium-confidence Codex background.)\n\nDesign: Penetrator dice are unchanged from the Godwyn anchor (6dx2(2) pi++; the subsonic load does not need to lose penetration to stay quiet), but the follow-up drops from the anchor's 3d cr ex to 2d cr ex, the same one-third cut as the old scale's 3d-to-2d: a subsonic round has less kinetic energy at impact to trigger a full-yield detonation of the internal charge. Handling: same Primaris-pattern housing weight class as the other two rifles above (23 lb loaded, min ST 15), with an integral suppressor and heavier barrel shroud pushing Bulk to -5 (worse than the standard Primaris bolt rifle's -4, matching the legacy Astartes pattern's figure) for the extra bulk that quiets the report. RoF 1 (single shots only, per its lore role as a precision weapon rather than a volume weapon) and Acc 6 - the best of any weapon on this page thanks to integral optics - reflect a rifle built to place one round exactly, not spray a squad's worth of fire.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
