		{
			"id": "elz-ZNiZCromC961U",
			"description": "Combi-Weapon, Bolter/Plasma",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Combi-weapons fuse a standard boltgun with a single-shot auxiliary barrel of a rarer special weapon, common Astartes wargear (especially for Chaplains, Sergeants and Deathwatch Space Marines) when a squad needs one extra answer to armour or a specific threat without giving up bolter fire entirely.\n\nDesign: The bolter barrel is the Godwyn anchor (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex) with a reduced magazine (20 vs 24) to make room for the auxiliary mechanism; the plasma barrel reuses the plasma gun's standard-mode damage line unchanged (6dx4(3) burn ex, see Plasma Weapons) since it is the same cartridge in a smaller reservoir, just good for one shot per reload. Handling: both barrels share one stock, so both usage lines carry the same handling figures. A full Astartes boltgun receiver plus a slaved plasma barrel and reservoir pushes total loaded weight to 42 lb - above the plain Godwyn-pattern boltgun's 38 lb, but well under carrying a separate boltgun and plasma pistol - and min ST to 19 (√(10×42)≈20.5, rounded to match the dominant bolter action). Bulk -5 matches a legacy Astartes boltgun's figure. RoF is per-mechanism, not copy-pasted: the bolter barrel keeps the standard semi/burst RoF 3, while the plasma barrel is RoF 1 (a single-shot auxiliary reservoir cannot cycle for a second pulse until reloaded) per framework.md's plasma-weapons rule.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
