		{
			"id": "eT5biDkkkJGXSdHxK",
			"description": "Combi-Weapon, Bolter/Melta",
			"local_notes": "Lore: As above; the melta-pattern auxiliary barrel is the combi-weapon most sought by squads expecting armour, since it turns a bolter-armed Space Marine into a one-shot tank-killer for the price of a single melta charge.\n\nDesign: Bolter barrel is the Godwyn anchor (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex). Melta barrel reuses the meltagun's short/beyond-½D damage split unchanged (8dx6(10) burn / 4dx6(3) burn beyond, see Melta Weapons) for a single shot, so the beyond-½D barrel carries the same multiplier and divisor as the meltagun's own beyond-½D formula. Handling: heaviest of the three combi-weapons at 44 lb loaded, since a melta reservoir and coil add more mass than the plasma barrel's reservoir does; min ST 20 (√(10×44)≈21, rounded to match the boltgun action's own housing) and Bulk -5 apply to every barrel, since they all share one stock. RoF is per-mechanism: bolter barrel RoF 3 (semi/burst), melta barrel RoF 1 at both range bands (melta weapons must recharge/vent between shots, per framework.md).",
