			"description": "Combi-Weapon, Bolter/Flamer",
			"local_notes": "Lore: As above; the flamer-pattern auxiliary is common on Sternguard and Deathwatch loadouts for clearing entrenched infantry without giving up ranged bolter fire.\n\nDesign: Bolter barrel is the Godwyn anchor (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 3d cr ex). Flamer barrel reuses the standard Flamer's damage (4d burn) and follow-up unchanged (see Flame Weapons) for a single one-shot fuel reservoir. Handling: lightest of the three combi-weapons at 40 lb loaded, since a promethium reservoir is lighter than a plasma or melta charge assembly; min ST 19 (√(10×40)≈20, rounded to match the boltgun's own housing) and Bulk -5 apply to both barrels. RoF is per-mechanism: bolter barrel RoF 3 (semi/burst), flamer barrel RoF 1 (a cone attack fired once per fuel charge, not a repeating weapon - see Flame Weapons).",
